# StoryLingo Supabase configuration for Vite
#
# 1. Open your Supabase project dashboard.
# 2. Go to Project Settings -> API.
# 3. Copy "Project URL" into VITE_SUPABASE_URL.
# 4. Copy the public "publishable" key into VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
# 5. Put real values in a local .env file or in your hosting provider environment variables.
#
# Do not commit real keys to GitHub.
# Do not use SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY or service_role keys in the frontend.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-supabase-publishable-key

# Legacy fallback, if your Supabase project still uses anon terminology:
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# Vercel Supabase integration may create these public variables:
# SUPABASE_URL
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#
# For Vite, prefer adding Vercel aliases:
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL = value of SUPABASE_URL
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = value of SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
